<span class="drop">M</span>y name's Matt Hanson, and I'm a senior journalism major at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. I was born and raised in the suburbs of Kansas City, and it was there that my passion for telling stories took root. At first I was all about fiction, writing a trio of short "novels" between the ages of 11 and 13. Later, as a sophomore at Shawnee Mission East High School in Prairie Village, Kansas, I started writing for the [award-winning](http://smeharbinger.net/about/awards/), The Harbinger, and found something I liked even more than fiction-writing: journalism.
I specialize in [data reporting](http://www.dailynebraskan.com/news/percent-of-new-unl-faculty-hired-since-work-part-time/article_41b00762-f496-11e5-9805-175cb6316494.html) and [web design](projects.dailynebraskan.com/letstalk) in my work for college publications and as an intern at professional outlets such as The Buffalo News and The Omaha World-Herald, where I am presently employed as a part-time data fellow.
